{"id": "tea:dasasloki:1", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The soul is of the nature of knowledge, dependent on Hari, fit to be joined with and separated from bodies, atomic, different in each body, a knower, and infinite in number.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda", "U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka", "tch:sankara"], "concepts": ["cpt:atomic-self", "cpt:jiva-as-part-of-brahman", "cpt:three-states-and-turiya"], "terms": ["trm:anu", "trm:cit"], "disputes": ["dsp:atomic-or-pervasive-self"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "practices": ["prc:neti-neti"], "notes": "Attributed to Śaṅkara (attribution traditional or disputed).", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda", "skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:10", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "10"}, "paraphrase": "The five things to be known by the wise: the nature of the one to be worshipped, of the worshipper, the fruit of grace, the rasa of devotion, and the nature of the obstacles to attaining him.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:arthapancaka-nimbarka"], "terms": ["trm:arthapancaka"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:2", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Souls are bound, their form covered by beginningless māyā, or released by the Lord's grace; the released are of different kinds.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:moksa"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:3", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "The non-conscious (acit) is of three kinds: the non-material (aprākṛta), the material (prākṛta) and time (kāla).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-realities-nimbarka"], "terms": ["trm:acit", "trm:aprakrta"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:4", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "4"}, "paraphrase": "Let us meditate on Kṛṣṇa, the lotus-eyed Hari, the supreme Brahman, who by nature is free of every fault, is the single mass of all auspicious qualities and has the vyūhas as his limbs.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "svabhāvato 'pāsta-samasta-doṣam aśeṣa-kalyāṇa-guṇaika-rāśim | vyūhāṅginaṃ brahma paraṃ vareṇyaṃ dhyāyema kṛṣṇaṃ kamalekṣaṇaṃ harim ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-realities-nimbarka"], "terms": ["trm:brahman"], "notes": "Verse number (4) moderate confidence; some editions may number differently.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:5", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "5"}, "paraphrase": "Let us remember the goddess, daughter of Vṛṣabhānu, shining joyfully on his left side, of matching beauty, always served by thousands of sakhīs, granting all desired ends.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:radha-hladini-sakti"], "terms": ["trm:yugala"], "disputes": ["dsp:status-of-radha"], "notes": "Among the earliest doctrinal texts to name Rādhā as the Lord's consort in worship.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:6", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "This (Brahman) is always to be worshipped by people for the removal of the darkness of ignorance; so it was taught by Sanandana and the other sages to Nārada, the witness of all truths.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka", "tch:narada"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:7", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "7"}, "paraphrase": "All knowledge is true, since according to scripture everything has Brahman as its self; the threefold nature (cit, acit, Īśvara) is established by scripture and the sūtras.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:svabhavika-bhedabheda", "cpt:three-realities-nimbarka"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:8", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "8"}, "paraphrase": "No other refuge is seen than Kṛṣṇa's lotus feet, worshipped by Brahmā, Śiva and the rest, who takes a form at his devotees' wish, whose power is inconceivable and whose intent is beyond thought.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "practices": ["prc:prapatti"], "terms": ["trm:prapatti"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasasloki:9", "source": "src:dasasloki", "location": {"ref": "9"}, "paraphrase": "His grace arises for one endowed with humility and the like; by it arises devotion marked by special love for the Lord who has no other master; that devotion is the highest (parā), and there is also the devotion that is a means (sādhana).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nimbarka"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-means-nimbarka"], "terms": ["trm:prema"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
